# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings: one rule for the whole repository.
#
#   * text=auto eol=lf
#     - text files are stored with LF in the repository AND checked out with LF
#       on every OS. Before this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows turned the whole
#       working tree into CRLF while the index stayed LF: `git status` was noisy
#       ("LF will be replaced by CRLF"), diffs depended on who edited the file,
#       and shell scripts shipped to fnOS (Linux) could break on their shebang.
#     - attributes always win over core.autocrlf, so the local config no longer
#       matters. Renormalize after changing this file:  git add --renormalize .
#     - files git detects as binary are left untouched; the explicit binary
#       rules below only make that guarantee unambiguous.
#   * cmd.exe batch scripts are the one exception that still needs CRLF.
#
# fnOS package scripts (fnos/offlineu/cmd/*, wizard/*, config/*, manifest, ...)
# are covered by the global rule - they run under fnOS's Linux shell.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command scripts must stay CRLF for cmd.exe.
*.bat               text eol=crlf
*.cmd               text eol=crlf

# Never touch line endings of binaries / archives.
*.png               binary
*.jpg               binary
*.jpeg              binary
*.gif               binary
*.ico               binary
*.webp              binary
*.svg               text
*.woff              binary
*.woff2             binary
*.ttf               binary
*.eot               binary
*.pdf               binary
*.zip               binary
*.gz                binary
*.tar               binary
*.fpk               binary
*.exe               binary
*.dll               binary
*.so                binary
*.wasm              binary
*.mp4               binary
*.mkv               binary
